<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>Hockey Training AI</title>
    <link
      rel="stylesheet"
      href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.7.2/css/all.min.css"
      integrity="sha512-Evv84Mr4kqVGRNSgIGL/F/aIDqQb7xQ2vcrdIwxfjThSH8CSR7PBEakCr51Ck+w+/U6swU2Im1vVX0SVk9ABhg=="
      crossorigin="anonymous"
      referrerpolicy="no-referrer" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/styles.css" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="/images/fav-icon.png" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <div class="hero">
      <div class="container">
        <nav class="nav">
          <div class="logo">
            <a href="/">🏋️‍♂️HockeyTrainingAI</a>
          </div>
          <div class="nav-btn-container">
            <button id="register-btn">Sign Up</button>
            <button id="login" class="login-btn">Login</button>
            <button id="dashboard-btn">Workouts</button>
          </div>
        </nav>

        <div class="hero-content">
          <h1 class="hero-title">Smarter off-ice training starts here</h1>
          <p class="hero-description">
            Get AI-generated workouts built for your hockey goals at fraction of
            the cost — no guesswork needed.
          </p>
          <div class="nav-btn-container">
            <button id="learn-more-btn">Learn More</button>
            <button class="get-started-btn">Get Started</button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="home-container">
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col" id="website-info">
          <img src="/images/battle-ropes.png" alt="" />
        </div>
        <div class="col">
          <h1>Smart Workouts, Built Just for you</h1>
          <p>
            Say goodbye to cookie-cutter routines. Fill out a quick form
            detailing your equipment, experience, age, and available time per
            session and let our AI do the heavy lifting. In seconds, you’ll
            receive a custom off-ice workout plan designed to help you reach
            your hockey goals efficiently, wherever you train.
          </p>
          <div class="center">
            <button class="get-started-btn">Sign Up</button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="home-container">
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col">
          <h1>Choose Your Phase:</h1>
          <h3>✅ 4 Weeks</h3>
          <h3>✅ 8 Weeks</h3>
          <h3>✅ 12 Weeks</h3>

          <p>
            Whether you're prepping for tryouts, rebuilding in the off-season,
            or staying sharp year-round, you can choose a training phase that
            fits your timeline. Each plan is structured for steady progression,
            giving you workouts that evolve as you do with intensity and goals
            tailored to your phase length.
          </p>
          <div class="center">
            <button class="get-started-btn">Sign Up</button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="col" id="website-info">
          <img src="/images/weeks-graph.png" alt="" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="home-container">
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col" id="website-info">
          <img src="/images/stockton-action-shot.jpg" alt="" />
        </div>
        <div class="col">
          <h1>Train Like a Hockey Player — Not a Bodybuilder</h1>
          <p>
            Every workout phase is designed with hockey performance in mind.
            Whether you're working on speed, strength, agility, or endurance,
            your plan includes drills and movements that directly translate to
            better performance on the ice. No fluff just focused off-ice
            training that fits your schedule and goals.
          </p>
          <div class="center">
            <button class="get-started-btn">Sign Up</button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </body>
  <script type="module" src="/js/main.js"></script>
</html>
